<title>COLOMBIA: Colombia boosts internal coffee price to new high.</title>
<headline>Colombia boosts internal coffee price to new high.</headline>
<text>
<p>BOGOTA, May 9 Reuter - Colombia's National Coffee Growers' Federation raised the country's internal coffee price for the 12th time since Jan. 31, setting it at a new high of 388,375 pesos per 125-kg load, a federation spokesman said.</p>
<p>The new price, up a razor-thin 0.02 percent from 387,625 per 125-kg load set on May 2, was based on an average trading price of $2.30 per pound of Colombian coffee in New York over the last 10 days.</p>
<p>The internal price has been cut only twice since Jan. 31, when a new sliding-scale formula was introduced to calculate payments to Colombian growers based on world market prices.</p>
<p>(-- Juan Guillermo Londono, Bogota newsroom, 571 610 7944)</p>
